## 6. Engineering Standards, Governance & Fitness Functions

This section serves as an adoptable multi-repository Engineering Standard.

### 6.1 Mandatory Standards vs. Context-Dependent Guidelines

| Rule ID | Standard / Guideline | Classification | Enforcement Mechanism |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **STD-01** | **No I/O Inside Domain Policies:** Modules under `**/domain/**` must never import ORM libraries, HTTP clients, or cloud SDKs. | **MANDATORY** | `dependency-cruiser` CI gate. |
| **STD-02** | **No External Network Calls Inside Open DB Transactions:** Never await third-party HTTP/gRPC calls (`Stripe`, `SendGrid`, `S3`) inside a `dataSource.transaction()` block. | **MANDATORY** | Code review + DB lock duration telemetry alert ($> 500\text{ms}$). |
| **STD-03** | **Strict Function Variance & Null Checks:** All `tsconfig.json` files must enable `"strict": true`, `"strictFunctionTypes": true`, and `"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true`. | **MANDATORY** | CI `tsc --noEmit` check. |
| **STD-04** | **Zero `as any` in Production or Test Suites:** Tests must use narrow ISP interfaces or factory builders rather than `{} as any`. | **MANDATORY** | ESLint `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any: "error"`. |
| **STD-05** | **DIP Ports for External Integrations:** All third-party external vendors (Payment, KYC, SMS, Storage) must sit behind a domain-owned Port interface. | **MANDATORY** | Architecture Review & PR Checklist. |
| **REC-01** | **OCP Strategy Registry:** Use multi-provider strategy registries when an integration or policy has $\ge 3$ concrete variants. | **RECOMMENDED** | Context-dependent (use exhaustive `switch` if variants are $\le 2$ or closed). |
| **REC-02** | **Repository Port Abstraction over ORM:** Abstract TypeORM/Prisma behind a `RepositoryPort` in core domain modules. | **CONTEXTUAL** | Required for complex domain modules; optional for simple CRUD/Admin modules. |

### 6.2 Technical Debt Classification & Refactoring Triggers

| Debt Severity | Concrete Signal / Trigger | Required Action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **P0 — Critical Architectural Hazard** | External HTTP/SDK call executed inside an open SQL transaction; or a subtype throwing `NotImplementedException` on a production path. | Block PR immediately; hotfix refactor before merge. |
| **P1 — High Coupling / Velocity Drag** | A single file modified by $\ge 3$ teams in the past 30 days with frequent merge conflicts; or unit test setup requiring $> 6$ mocks. | Allocate refactoring story in the current sprint before adding new features to that module. |
| **P2 — Moderate Smell** | React component exceeding 250 lines mixing data normalization and presentation; or `switch` statement modified for a 3rd integration variant. | Refactor opportunistically via the Boy Scout Rule when touching the file next. |
| **P3 — Cosmetic / Benign** | Internal helper class injected concretely instead of via an interface when it performs no I/O. | **Do not refactor.** Leave as-is to avoid churn. |

